LocalizedStrings.enGB:
{n}Lann and Wenduag stare in utter shock, their bitter feud halted in its tracks by the sheer weight of your command.{/n}

"You... you cannot be serious," {n}Lann stammers, lowering his bow in disbelief.{/n} "Us? Together?"

{n}Wenduag shivers, a mixture of predatory awe and subservience gleaming in her eyes.{/n} "Power dictates the law of the caves. If you have the strength to bend us both to your will, {mf|master|mistress}... then neither of us can refuse."

"Every cup! EVERY cup! You madman, you actually did it."

{n}He pulls a scroll out of nowhere, scribbles on it with a quill of candle flame and flicks it into the air, where it burns into a little crown of stars.{/n}

"A deal is a deal, and I only break the boring ones. Tell the Cosmic Store you want to be my Avatar, and you pay half: 5,000 Cosmic Coins instead of 10,000. You still have to follow me as your patron, of course. I am generous, not stupid."

"Ah, the Stolen Lands. My masterpiece! I wrote that little kingdom a fairy tale: an exiled queen, a cursed wood, a hundred tragic endings. And then that ruler of yours tore up the script, marched into the House at the End of Time and finished my Nyrissa's story on their terms instead of mine. The ratings were magnificent. I have still not forgiven them."

{n}He sniffs the air around you, delighted.{/n}

"You carry a little of that ruler's shadow, you know. The Wild Hunt could smell it on the sands, and so could I."

"Because it should feel familiar! You have climbed off that festival stretcher before, kid. Once, twice, a hundred times? I do not count. I only keep score. The counting is done by the one who is both the Key and the Gate, and doors are its whole business. You came through one, did you not?"

{n}He taps the side of his nose.{/n}

"Ask yourself who gains when a story is told again and again. Then ask why the audience keeps paying for tickets. That is two hints, which is two more than the Inheritor will ever give you."

"Done and dusted! Spend it on something tasteless."

{n}He leans in and drops his voice to a conspiratorial whisper.{/n}

"And here is a secret deal, just between us and every god who is listening. Win every cup on these sands, every last one, and I will let you become my Avatar at the Cosmic Store for half the price. Half! Nobody gets half. Well. You might."
